A recursive approach compares first and last characters and reduces the problem size.

boolean isPalindrome(String str, int start, int end) {
    if (start >= end) return true;
    if (str.charAt(start) != str.charAt(end)) return false;
    return isPalindrome(str, start + 1, end - 1);
}

Each term is the sum of previous two terms.

int fib(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2);
}

Sort both strings and compare.

boolean isAnagram(String s1, String s2) {
    char[] a = s1.toCharArray();
    char[] b = s2.toCharArray();
    Arrays.sort(a);
    Arrays.sort(b);
    return Arrays.equals(a, b);
}

Factorial can be calculated recursively.

int factorial(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * factorial(n-1);
}

Use sum formula n(n+1)/2.

int findMissing(int[] arr, int n) {
    int sum = n * (n + 1) / 2;
    for (int num : arr) sum -= num;
    return sum;
}

Repeatedly sum digits until a single digit remains.

int sumDigits(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    return n % 10 + sumDigits(n / 10);
}

boolean isMagic(int n) {
    while (n > 9) {
        n = sumDigits(n);
    }
    return n == 1;
}

